like we have in the past, we're not going to be able to get the payload in the space

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:39.250
like we want to. We're studying here the fundamental physics of buckling and then

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:43.940
trying to apply that to an updated design criteria that will allow us to

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:48.780
make us lighter weight, more efficient, safe launch vehicle strutting. I've got a

